error[E0277]: `NotADialect` is not a tokora dialect
  --> tests/ui/dialect.rs:12:19
   |
12 |   needs_dialect::<NotADialect>();
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^ this type has no `Dialect` impl, so its lexer and language brand are unknown
   |
help: the trait `Dialect<'_>` is not implemented for `NotADialect`
  --> tests/ui/dialect.rs:7:1
   |
 7 | struct NotADialect;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: a dialect is one impl naming the two things a production cannot derive: `impl<'inp, Src> Dialect<'inp> for MyDialect<Src> { type Lang = MyLang; type Lexer = MyLexer<'inp, Src>; }`
   = note: everything else — source, slice, token, span, offset, token capabilities — is reachable by projection from `Lexer`, so pin those in a one-line subtrait (`trait MyDialectBound<'inp>: Dialect<'inp, Lang = MyLang, Lexer: Lexer<'inp, …>> {}`) rather than as further associated items
note: required by a bound in `needs_dialect`
  --> tests/ui/dialect.rs:9:27
   |
 9 | fn needs_dialect<'inp, D: Dialect<'inp>>() {}
   |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `needs_dialect`
